esis which favored C on parse-today grounds. Maintainer note: \"we are building a new language and it''s in the early stages; most feature requests do not assume this will already parse and that is natural\" -- i.e. A''s three novel surfaces (new fn-declaration shape, return-type inference, type-name-as-match-call expression form) are accepted design cost, not disqualifying. Build task: implement A. gh:152 to be closed on landing.'\nplans/incidents/issue-169-20260901/20260901-010814-issue-169.jsonl.tail:34:{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1788217712747,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fa5eb6461ffeMsD7uLAy4rsiUF\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"bash\",\"callID\":\"chatcmpl-tool-ad6d7ae8b4a63a12\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"id:\\\" plans/board.yaml | head -80\"},\"output\":\"1:- id: sink-kind-build\\n9:- id: function-signature-matching-syntax\\n17:- id: declare-terminator-build\\n25:- id: jsonlines-tail-marker-build\\n33:- id: dsv-partial-conventions\\n41:- id: euler-slow-fragments-2\\n49:- id: variant-types-flip\\n57:- id: shell-out-build\\n64:- id: stdin-redesign-build\\n72:- id: overloading-and-traits-design\\n78:- id: mutation-semantics-design\\n85:- id: float-build\\n92:- id: benchmark-suite-build\\n99:- id: lines-utf8-edge\\n106:- id: rust-lines-tl-fail-build\\n114:- id: retire-ternary-build\\n122:- id: search-layer-build\\n128:- id: sort-by-max-by\\n134:- id: param-destructure-build\\n140:- id: bigint-tracking\\n148:- id: js-node-web-split-build\\n155:- id: module-as-function-routing-design\\n163:- id: erlang-target-consideration\\n171:- id: variant-checker-capital-first\\n178:- id: match-type-wrapper-experiment\\n185:- id: partial-application-system-design\\n194:- id: draft-core-model-migration\\n203:- id: draft-access-model-migration\\n211:- id: draft-numbers-operators-migration\\n219:- id: draft-records-migration\\n227:- id: draft-streams-migration\\n235:- id: draft-calls-modules-migration\\n243:- id: draft-matchi