{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788382946157,"sessionID":"ses_f9c130ecaffeXIzoGLIIVyKiu4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a6aa26bef0eac130","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"ls src/check/ && echo \"---\" && wc -l src/check/*.rs src/parse.rs src/tir.rs src/ty.rs"},"output":"linearity.rs\nmod.rs\ntypes.rs\n---\n   328 src/check/linearity.rs\n  3239 src/check/mod.rs\n   556 src/check/types.rs\n  1509 src/parse.rs\n   612 src/tir.rs\n   496 src/ty.rs\n  6740 total\n","metadata":{"output":"linearity.rs\nmod.rs\ntypes.rs\n---\n   328 src/check/linearity.rs\n  3239 src/check/mod.rs\n   556 src/check/types.rs\n  1509 src/parse.rs\n   612 src/tir.rs\n   496 src/ty.rs\n  6740 total\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"ls src/check/ && echo \"---\" && wc -l src/check/*.rs src/parse.rs src/tir.rs src/ty.rs","time":{"start":1788382946155,"end":1788382946156}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"This is a big task. Let me understand the plan. Option A is: `fn render = Msg(Ping -> \"*ping*\" or Quit -> \"*quit*\" or Text -> .body)`.\n\nThe function declaration shape changes to: `fn <name> = <body>` where the body is a \"type-name-as-match-call\" expression form. The match is over the single input `.` (implicit parameter).\n\nThree novel surfaces:\n1. New fn-declaration shape: `fn <name> = <match-call-expr>` (no explicit params list, no return annotation)\n2. Return-type inference from match arms\n3. Type-name-as-match-call expression form: `Msg(Ping -> ... or Quit -> ...)` where Msg is a variant type used like a call, the match is over the input `.`.\n\nLet me think about how this should work semantically. The idea (from the maintainer's sketch in the issue): the whole function becomes a matcher. `.` is always the input value. `Msg(...)` marks the type of the input (Msg) AND the destructuring rules via the match arms.\n\nSo `fn render = Msg(Ping -> \"*ping*\" or Quit -> \"*quit*\" or Text -> .body)` is a function that takes a `Msg` value and returns a `Str`. The match arms destructure the input.\n\nActually wait - let me reconsider. The type-name-as-match-call: `Msg(Ping -> ... or Quit -> ...)`. Here `Msg` is the type name, and inside the parens is a match. But what are `Ping`, `Quit`, `Text`? They are variant constructors of the `Msg` enum. The match is over the input `.` which is a `Msg`.\n\nSo the semantics: The function's parameter is implicitly `.`, its type is `Msg`. The body is the match over `.`. Return type inferred from arms.\n\nLet me look at how matching works, enums, and the check module. This is a large task, so let me be systematic. Let me look at the check module structure and how Def is checked.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_063ee21fa001KA3NW8c6SgcNFB","sessionID":"ses_f9c130ecaffeXIzoGLIIVyKiu4","messageID":"msg_063edf9bb0013q10v4PPFqoVNN"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788382946901,"sessionID":"ses_f9c130ecaffeXIzoGLIIVyKiu4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-ae40752c06b59da1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"fn.*def\\|check_def\\|fn check\\|Def\\b\\|def_ret\\|def.body\\|def.ret\\|def.param\" src/check/mod.rs | head -40"},"output":"104:pub fn check(file: &File) -> Result<tir::Program, Error> {\n210:    funcs.extend(check_defs(own_defs, &ctx)?);\n297:/// `ctx`'s own per-def fields (`scope`, `subject`, `in_fn`, ...) are ignored -- each def gets its\n299:fn check_defs<'a>(\n300:    defs: impl IntoIterator<Item = &'a crate::ast::Def>,\n306:        let scope = match (&def.param, &sig.param) {\n323:            in_fn: Some(&def.name),\n338:            if matches!(def.body, Expr::TailPipe { .. }) {\n339:                tail_pipe(&def_ctx, &def.body)?\n340:            } else if let Some(tir) = sink_call(&def_ctx, &def.body)? {\n344:                    def.body.span(),\n353:            match expect_inner(&def_ctx, &def.body, &sig.ret)? {\n358:        if let Some(param) = &def.param {\n359:            check_param(&body, param, &sig.param, &def.name, def.body.span())?;\n363:                def.body.span(),\n372:            param: def.param.as_ref().map(|p| p.name.clone()),\n384:pub fn check_module(module: &crate::ast::Module) -> Result<Vec<tir::Func>, Error> {\n440:    check_defs(module.defs.iter(), &ctx)\n447:fn check_param(\n480:fn check_program_body(ctx: &Ctx, body: &Expr) -> Result<Tir, Error> {\n1192:/// `check_defs`'s `expect_inner`, and the body's type is whatever the block's value expression is.\n1251:fn check_reachable(\n1283:fn check_coverage(\n1756:        // which `check_program_body` and `check_defs` handle before `synth` is reached. A `Sink`\n","metadata":{"output":"104:pub fn check(file: &File) -> Result<tir::Program, Error> {\n210:    funcs.extend(check_defs(own_defs, &ctx)?);\n297:/// `ctx`'s own per-def fields (`scope`, `subject`, `in_fn`, .